# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the fusion programme's WP1 jobs (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the fusion integration branch and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from here. ONE IMAGE FOR THE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the
# tag the integrator's build job produces from the integration commit (sed -i 's/tp4-fusion-1/<tag>/' *.env); a commit of a file the image carries needs a new build and tag.
# These jobs add to the generated pack in scripts/ci/references/fusion-jobs (make_fusion_jobs.py: <ID>A audited attach and the timed ABAB of the one-core fold, lever id s1): the card-M job
# C1 that runs FIRST, the tree-fold variants (lever twins s1f2) and the trace_ms read of the ABAB.
# A1b: the AUDITED four-card attach of S1 (tree fold) on c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s1f2-audit, the production profile (Lever N + prefix reuse + W2 + engine reuse) plus QWEN_FAST_TP4_SHARD_ARGMAX=1 and QWEN_FAST_TP4_SHARD_ARGMAX_FOLD2=1 and its audit
# QWEN_FAST_TP4_SHARD_ARGMAX_AUDIT=1 (a gate-only twin: scripts/ci/fusion-wp/WP1.json, placed by make_fusion_profiles.py). Today's Untilize + ArgMax + Gather runs beside the kernels in every verify capture and every round compares every
# row of every chip: ids exactly, values as numbers (-0 == +0, NaN with NaN), and the joined words tensor against the kernel's own ids and value bits.
# READ in this order and stop at the first failure: (1) '[PINDIAG] tp4 shard argmax engaged rows=64 workers=<W> tasks=<2W> fold=2 audit=1 words=1' (W = 110 or 130, the grid the card exposes) and NO 'fell back' line
# (tp4_shard_argmax_smoke.problems does both); (2) '[PINDIAG] tp4 shard argmax audit <n> exact=True rows=64 chips=4' lines and NONE 'audit mismatch' (a mismatch names round, chip, rows, kernel and served ids; a 'words rows=[..]'
# mismatch is the joined tensor disagreeing with the kernel's own ids/values); (3) c2_smoke_check clean; (4) every answer's content hash equal to the control's on concurrent8_code_32k and concurrent8_code_equal.
# The audit's served path adds launches to the verify capture (the cost every audited lever pays); the hang shapes are the integrator's, not this job's. Duration (estimate): 60 min. Stop rule.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-s1f2-audit
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k,concurrent8_code_equal
